---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Exbound's mission, principles, and scope: independent, compatible, open reconstructions of proprietary scientific and engineering software."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Independent, compatible, open</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Exbound reconstructs proprietary, abandoned, and monopolized scientific
        and engineering software as independent applications that are compatible
        with the originals.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Principles</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Compatibility, not cloning.</strong> We reimplement what the
            software does and describe it by compatibility — never copying vendor
            code, artwork, or trademarks, and never naming an implementation
            after a product.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Evidence over assertion.</strong> Claims carry the command or
            source that produced them; compatibility is claimed only when
            verified against documented reference behavior.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Lawful and clean-room.</strong> Work proceeds only on
            lawfully held copies, with a documented clean-room method where a
            proprietary original is involved.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Reproducibility as the core standard.</strong> Public setup,
            tests that don't require proprietary software, and issues that state
            what correctness means.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Scope</h2>
        <p>
          Exbound is for interoperability and preservation. It does not defeat
          DRM, dongles, or activation on currently sold software, and does not
          distribute circumvention tools. See the
          <a href="https://github.com/exbound/.github/blob/main/SECURITY.md"
            >security &amp; scope policy</a
          >
          and the
          <a href="https://github.com/exbound/research/blob/main/docs/legal-basis.md"
            >legal basis</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Governance</h2>
        <p>
          Founder-led and deliberately lightweight. Write access is earned
          through a track record of evidence-backed contributions. See
          <a href="https://github.com/exbound/.github/blob/main/GOVERNANCE.md"
            >governance</a
          >.
        </p>

        <p>
          Exbound is not affiliated with, authorized by, or endorsed by any
          software vendor. Product names are used only to describe
          compatibility.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
